    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d662">

                <pb facs="0736" n="724" xml:id="pg724"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">890G.00/518: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Minister Resident in Iraq</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Knabenshue</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the
                        Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Baghdad</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1940-12-18T19:00:00+03:00">December 18,
                            1940—7 p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received 11:40 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>123. I was informed today by the chief British intelligence officer that the
                    Regent called the members of the Cabinet to him yesterday and declared to them
                    that the best interests of the state required their immediate resignations. The
                    Prime Minister replied that he would consider the matter.</p>
                <p>It is expected that a decision will be made within a few days. The attitude of
                    the army is still an important factor, perhaps the most important.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Knabenshue</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
